SUMMARY:Deadline: ERA:AI Fellowship 2027 (Winter cohort\, Cambridge)
DESCRIPTION:Paid in-person research fellowship in Cambridge for people who 
 want to build expertise in AI safety or AI governance. Fellows develop and
  complete a research project on mitigating risks from frontier AI\, workin
 g in one of three streams: technical safety\, governance\, or technical AI
  governance. WHAT YOU GET: a GBP 10\,000 stipend for the 10-week programme
 \, visa support\, travel expense coverage\, meals during working hours\, e
 xpert mentorship from established researchers\, dedicated research managem
 ent support aimed at publishing in top venues\, and immersion in Cambridge
 's AI safety research community with regular social and networking events.
  Top performers can be extended by 6 months or more through the Research S
 cholars programme. ELIGIBILITY: open to anyone 18 or older\; the programme
  is talent-first with no formal credential requirement\, welcoming researc
 hers\, students and professionals from technical\, policy\, security\, leg
 al\, economic and other relevant backgrounds\; prior formal research exper
 ience is not required. SELECTION: three stages\, a written application of 
 roughly 2 hours\, Round 1 interviews in late September for the top 20 perc
 ent\, and Round 2 interviews in early October. COHORT: starts 18 January 2
 027. Deadline 13 September 2026 at 23:59 Anywhere on Earth.\n\nOrganisatio
 n: ERA Fellowship\nLocation: Cambridge\, United Kingdom\, in person with d
 edicated desk space at ERA's office. Visa support provided.\nAward: GBP 10
 \,000 stipend for the 10-week fellowship\, plus visa support\, travel expe
 nse coverage and meals during working hours. Top performers can receive 6+
  month extensions through the Research Scholars programme. No application 
 fee.\nDuration: 10 weeks\, 18 January to late March 2027. Deadline 13 Sept
 ember 2026 at 23:59 Anywhere on Earth.\n\nMore: https://erafellowship.org/
 fellowship?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://erafellowship.org/fellowship?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Cambridge\, United Kingdom\, in person with dedicated desk space a
 t ERA's office. Visa support provided.
END:VEVENT
