  Fellow to work with its Head of Governance at the intersection of AI eval
 uation\, policy and governance. RESPONSIBILITIES: defining standards and b
 est practices for independent AI oversight (including the AI Evaluator For
 um and the AEF-1 standard for evaluator independence)\, developing partner
 ships for interdisciplinary AI evaluations (for example on AI impacts on s
 elf-harm\, suicide risk\, mania and psychosis)\, engaging government and p
 olicy stakeholders (including the U.S. Center for AI Standards and Innovat
 ion\, the EU AI Office and the UK AI Security Institute)\, and translating
  technical research on reinforcement learning and interpretability for pol
 icymakers\, journalists and the public. PROFILE: hybrid technical and poli
 cy background\; technical fluency in AI evaluation\, hands-on policy or le
 gal experience related to AI\, academic research experience\, and strong c
 ommunication skills\; domain experience in mental health\, child safety\, 
 fraud\, political persuasion or consumer protection is a plus. Based in Sa
 n Francisco with in-person work expected\; visa sponsorship available. Rol
 ling applications.\n\nOrganisation: Transluce\nLocation: San Francisco\, U
 S\, in office. International visa sponsorship possible.\nAward: USD 200\,0
 00 to 300\,000 per year salary plus benefits. Full-time\; part-time possib
 le for exceptional candidates.\nDuration: Full-time position (part-time op
 portunities available for exceptional candidates).\n\nMore: https://jobs.g
 em.com/transluce/am9icG9zdDpVz8DJmgMdoy_WaOqlBt2o?utm_source=artificialnou
