DTSTAMP:20261026T135004Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: Pivotal Research Fellowship (2027 Q1)
DESCRIPTION:Fully funded\, full-time\, in-person research fellowship in Lon
 don for anyone 18 or over committed to ensuring AI develops safely. Fellow
 s work on a project with an established mentor\, with weekly 1-on-1s\, ded
 icated research-management support and co-working at LISA. Past projects s
 pan AI governance\, technical AI safety and technical AI governance. Among
  this round's projects\, Risto Uuk and a co-mentor are supervising a fello
 w on EU AI governance\, looking for someone curious and motivated with exp
 erience or interest in policy or law. Other mentors include Patrick Leverm
 ore\, Alexandra Abbas\, Caspar Kaiser\, Cecilia Elena Tilli\, Connor Dunlo
 p\, Daniel Tan and Dave Banerjee\; the full list is on the fellowship page
 .\n\nOrganisation: Pivotal Research\nLocation: London (London Initiative f
 or Safe AI / LISA). In person\; meeting UK entry requirements is the fello
 w's responsibility\, though Pivotal offers visa guidance and can sometimes
  help.\nAward: £15\,000 to £18\,000 stipend (£18\,000 for senior fellow
 s\, e.g. PhD\, industry track record or strong publications) + travel to a
 nd from London + £1\,800/month housing for non-London fellows + weekday l
 unch and dinner + compute.\nDuration: 15 weeks full-time (18 January to 30
  April 2027)\n\nMore: https://www.pivotal-research.org/fellowships/ai-safe
 ty-fellowship?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.pivotal-research.org/fellowships/ai-safety-fellowship?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:London (London Initiative for Safe AI / LISA). In person\; meeting
  UK entry requirements is the fellow's responsibility\, though Pivotal off
 ers visa guidance and can sometimes help.
END:VEVENT
