DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: Generator Residency (Kairos x Constellation\, Winter 2027
 )
DESCRIPTION:A three-month residency for AI safety generalists: builders\, o
 perators and organizers rather than researchers. Residents pitch\, build a
 nd ship their own projects with weekly advice from field leaders\, then ge
 t support landing a full-time AI safety role. ELIGIBILITY: open worldwide 
 to early- and mid-career people from operations\, communications\, policy\
 , engineering\, computer science and similar fields\; the main criteria ar
 e a track record of execution and a genuine commitment to AI safety. TIMEL
 INE: applications close end of day 1 November 2026 (Anywhere on Earth)\; i
 nternational applicants are strongly encouraged to apply by 26 October for
  visa time. Work tests by 9 November\, interviews mid-November\, decisions
  by 25 November. Free-response answers must be written without AI assistan
 ce.\n\nOrganisation: Kairos and Constellation\nLocation: Berkeley\, Califo
 rnia\, USA (Constellation office). Core residency is in person\; J-1 visa 
 sponsorship available for most international applicants.\nAward: USD 8\,50
 0 per month stipend (some Embedded track residents employed at a roughly e
 quivalent salary)\, plus travel to and from Berkeley. No application fee.\
 nDuration: 3 months full-time (18 January to 9 April 2027)\; selected resi
 dents can extend in person until late May and remotely until early July 20
 27.\n\nMore: https://generatorresidency.org/?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://generatorresidency.org/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berkeley\, California\, USA (Constellation office). Core residency
  is in person\; J-1 visa sponsorship available for most international appl
 icants.
END:VEVENT
