DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261102
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261103
SUMMARY:Deadline: BRAID Creative Commissions 2027: A Promise in Return (Res
 ponsible AI\, GBP 8\,000-12\,000\, Edinburgh Art Festival)
DESCRIPTION:BRAID\, the UKRI AHRC-funded Responsible AI programme at the Un
 iversity of Edinburgh\, is commissioning around seven creative works that 
 treat Responsible AI as a question of relationships\, commitments and obli
 gations rather than a technical checklist or a set of rules\, under the ti
 tle A Promise in Return. WHO: UK-based creative practitioners in any mediu
 m: artists\, designers\, musicians and performers\, architects and urban d
 esigners\, craftspeople and artisans\, writers and poets. Full-time underg
 raduate and taught postgraduate students are not eligible\; PhD students m
 ay apply if registered as self-employed freelancers. WHAT YOU GET: a commi
 ssion budget of GBP 8\,000 to 12\,000\, production support from Inspace an
 d the Institute for Design Informatics\, and presentation during the Edinb
 urgh Art Festival in August 2027 with the Edinburgh Futures Institute. APP
 LICATION: online form (written or an eight-minute video application) plus 
 a single PDF of portfolio\, CV and budget emailed to braid@ed.ac.uk\; late
  submissions are not accepted. DEADLINE: Monday 2 November 2026 at 17:00 G
 MT.\n\nOrganisation: BRAID (Bridging Responsible AI Divides)\, University 
 of Edinburgh\, with Inspace\, the Institute for Design Informatics and the
  Edinburgh Futures Institute\nLocation: UK. For UK-based creative practiti
 oners\; work is presented in Edinburgh during the Edinburgh Art Festival\,
  August 2027.\nAward: Around seven commissions with budgets of GBP 8\,000 
 to 12\,000 each\, inclusive of VAT and all costs. No application fee.\nDur
 ation: Projects run January to August 2027\, presented during the Edinburg
 h Art Festival in August 2027\, with possible further displays through 202
 8.\n\nMore: https://braiduk.org/creative-commissions?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://braiduk.org/creative-commissions?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:UK. For UK-based creative practitioners\; work is presented in Edi
 nburgh during the Edinburgh Art Festival\, August 2027.
END:VEVENT
